id: pm-jtwsct
title: "GH-920: health conflates lossless merge receipts with discarded-value decisions"
description: "health counts every pending merge receipt as a blocking merge decision even when the field-aware merge preserved both agents' changes, training agents to clear the same signal that protects against genuine data loss."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-07T08:33:39.644Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T08:47:22.284Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: Health reports lossless reconciliation receipts separately from decisions that discard a competing value; severity and recovery guidance are derived from the receipt semantics rather than filename or authoring path; paired merge fixtures and fresh-clone validation prove both classes without weakening history checks
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
expected_result: "Strict health blocks on discarded-value decisions, reports lossless receipts separately, and names discarded fields so the signal is actionable."
actual_result: Lossless and lossy receipts both increment pending_merge_decisions and fail strict health with no classification in the health envelope.
affected_version: 2026.8.5
component: merge health and receipt classification
